---
// The three claims on the home page. Numbers are from docs/test-images.md §6; change
// them only when that table changes.
import { url } from '../lib/url';

const benchmark = 'https://github.com/cruzzil/arcsec/blob/main/docs/test-images.md#6-results--103-images-arcsec-vs-astap';
---

<ul class="proof not-content" aria-label="Why arcsec">
	<li>
		<p class="figure"><span class="big">90</span><span class="of">of 103</span></p>
		<p class="what">benchmark images solved correctly</p>
		<p class="detail">
			ASTAP solved 47 given the same position hints and field sizes. Every solve is checked against the
			known coordinates at the centre and all four corners. <a href={benchmark}>Benchmark details</a>
		</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<p class="figure"><span class="big">0</span><span class="of">false positives</span></p>
		<p class="what">across the same benchmark</p>
		<p class="detail">
			A reported solve more than 5″ out at any corner counts as wrong. Five of the images are deliberate
			traps, tiny crops of nebula and galaxy cores that should not solve; arcsec reports no solution rather than
			inventing one.
		</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<p class="figure"><span class="big word">N.I.N.A.</span></p>
		<p class="what">works as its “ASTAP” solver</p>
		<p class="detail">
			Same flags, same <code>.ini</code> and <code>.wcs</code> files, same exit codes. Point N.I.N.A. at{" "}
			<code>arcsec.exe</code> and keep your ASTAP star databases. <a href={url('nina/')}>Set-up guide</a>
		</p>
	</li>
</ul>

<style>
	.proof {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
	}
	li {
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	p {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.figure {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
	.big {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-5xl);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.big.word {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-4xl);
	}
	.of {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.what {
		margin-top: 0.35rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.detail {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.detail a {
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
	}
</style>
